M1: `pose` -> `movement` (synchronized head tilt + wrist tilt). M2: `pose` -> `movement` (wrist tilt) -> `movement` (head tilt). Winner: M1, because synchronizing the head and hand movements into a single, cohesive action creates a much stronger and more natural-looking questioning gesture.
